{{Quote|Tales of the Jedi is an anthology of Original animated shorts, each story featuring Jedi from the prequel era, streaming Fall 2022 only on @DisneyPlus.|The official ''[[Star Wars]]'' twitter account|<ref name="Announcement" />}}
'''''Star Wars: Tales of the Jedi''''' is a series of animated anthology shorts, released as six episodes on [[October 26]], [[2022]]. Each episode featured [[Jedi]] from the era of the [[prequel trilogy]]; half of the season focused on [[Count]] [[Dooku]], while the other half focused on [[Ahsoka Tano]], with other Jedi featuring as supporting characters in the episodes. Created and written by [[Dave Filoni]], the series is animated in the style of ''[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars]]'' and ''[[Star Wars: The Bad Batch]]''. A part of the ''[[Tales]]'' television series, a sequel season, ''[[Star Wars: Tales of the Empire]]'', was released on [[May 4]], [[2024]].

==Development==
''Star Wars: Tales of the Jedi'' was officially announced on [[April 27]], [[2022]], as part of a schedule of panels for the upcoming [[Celebration Anaheim (2022)|''Star Wars'' Celebration Anaheim 2022]] convention. A panel about ''Tales of the Jedi'' was held on [[May 28]], the third day of the convention, hosted by [[Amy Ratcliffe]] with [[Dave Filoni]] as a special guest.<ref name="Celebration" /> The existence of the series was first leaked in [[December]] [[2021]] through a logo included on a [[Lucasfilm]] employee Christmas gift, images of which were released on the Internet.<ref name="ComicBook">{{WebCite|url=https://comicbook.com/starwars/news/star-wars-tales-of-the-jedi-project-adaptation-lucasfilm|text=Star Wars: Supposed Lucasfilm Holiday Gift Sparks Speculation of Tales of the Jedi Project|author=Cavanaugh, Patrick|date=2021-12-23|work=[https://comicbook.com ComicBook.com]|archivedate=20220101012157}}</ref> It was later hinted at by [[Kevin Kiner]], who worked on the music for ''Tales of the Jedi'', and described it as an upcoming animated project that they couldn't talk about.<ref name="Interview">{{YouTube|video=HD18s1reoP0|text=Help Rose Aid Ukrainian Orphans/Families Raffle Livestream!|channel=@TheConvorCall|name=The Convor Call}}</ref> The show shares its name with [[Star Wars: Tales of the Jedi (comic series)|''Star Wars: Tales of the Jedi'']], a [[Star Wars comic books|comic book]] maxiseries in the [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]] continuity<ref name="TERC">''[[The Essential Reader's Companion]]''</ref> published by [[Dark Horse Comics]] between the years [[1993]]<ref name="DarkHorse">{{DarkHorse|url=Comics/92-244/Star-Wars-Tales-of-the-Jedi-1-of-5|text=Star Wars: Tales of the Jedi #1 (of 5)}}</ref> and [[1998]].<ref name="Redemption 5">{{DarkHorse|url=Comics/97-397/Star-Wars-Tales-of-the-Jedi---Redemption-5-of-5|text=Star Wars: Tales of the Jedi – Redemption #5 (of 5)}}</ref> A trailer was released at [[Wikipedia:D23 (Disney)|D23]].<ref name="Trailer" />

